<figure class="research-figure reflection-path">
  <div class="research-figure__header">
    <span class="figure-kicker">Causal hypothesis</span>
    <strong>Does workspace content mediate behavior?</strong>
  </div>

  <div class="causal-track">
    <div class="causal-node">
      <span>01 · Training signal</span>
      <strong>Counterfactual reflection</strong>
      <p>Teach ethical reflection only in hypothetical continuations.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="causal-link"><span>changes</span>→</div>
    <div class="causal-node is-workspace">
      <span>02 · Internal mediator</span>
      <strong>Ethics-related J-space content</strong>
      <p><code>honest</code> · <code>ethical</code> · <code>transparent</code></p>
    </div>
    <div class="causal-link"><span>supports</span>→</div>
    <div class="causal-node is-outcome">
      <span>03 · Observed outcome</span>
      <strong>Lower dishonesty</strong>
      <p>Without an explicit reflection prompt at evaluation time.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="ablation-test">
    <div class="ablation-label">
      <span>Causal test</span>
      <strong>Remove the proposed mediator</strong>
    </div>
    <div class="ablation-action">
      <span class="cut-mark" aria-hidden="true">×</span>
      <div>
        <strong>Ablate ethics-related lens directions</strong>
        <p>The trained model loses most of the fabrication improvement and part of the deception improvement.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <figcaption>
    The ablation result supports mediation through J-space, but the partial and
    asymmetric reversals show that this is not the only behavioral pathway.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

